{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The memory cards fit my repeated use of removable storage across devices. The two-pack gives me useful spares, provided the cards are compatible.",
    "The HDMI cable fits a possible connection need between my DVD player and TV, although I would check their ports and the cable length before choosing it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo displays and smart plug introduce Alexa features I have not shown a need for; owning a Fire tablet does not mean I want home automation or another screen.",
    "The newer Fire tablets largely duplicate a device I already own, while the streaming stick serves a different purpose from the disc playback I recently bought a DVD player for.",
    "Echo Auto does not address the practical mounting, charging, and connectivity needs behind my car accessory purchases."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire tablet purchase seems to have been treated as broad interest in Amazon devices and Alexa.",
    "My purchases of electronics seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest more devices, even when I usually need accessories for equipment I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly buy specific supporting items such as memory cards, cables, mounts, and storage cases, so usefulness with my existing equipment matters to me.",
    "Compatibility matters more than sharing a brand: the memory-card two-pack appeals because I could use it across suitable devices.",
    "My latest lens-cap purchase continues my camera accessory needs, which these recommendations barely address."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my storage and connection needs but read too much interest in Alexa devices and replacements into my existing electronics purchases."
}"}
